# Tapping I again on a rail without a new direction is no switch: the same
# grind again used to end the entry and start another, stacking "BS 50-50 + BS 50-50 + ..." with a
# multiplier each. Five plain taps during a 50-50 on the lab ledge now leave one 50-50. A real
# switch (I + a direction into a different grind) still counts (lab-grind-switch), after
# grind.switchTicks (20) on the grind it leaves.
park lab
cmd 0 teleport 0 -0.6 0.14 90
hold up 6..100
hold ollie 90..105
tap grind 176
tap grind 200
tap grind 215
tap grind 230
tap grind 245
tap grind 260
bot balance
run 560
expect event grindStart{trick=BS 50-50} within 175..179
expect event grindStart count == 1
expect event grindEnd{trick=BS 50-50,reason=end} within 400..404
expect event comboLanded{name=BS 50-50,multiplier=1,points=475} within 465..469
expect no event bail
